{"root_cause":"The _onBeforeShow() method in drawer.ts only initializes swipe gestures but does not move focus into the drawer when it opens. Keyboard users cannot interact with the drawer's content because focus remains on the trigger button or body.","repair_strategy":"Override _onBeforeShow() to focus the drawer's dismiss button (identified by the standard data-bs-dismiss="drawer" attribute) after initializing swipe. This works generically across all pages using the drawer component.","edits":[{"path":"js/src/drawer.ts","sha256":"ec1263ee997c9acf245a67902c7e977f7550be6b313ada12b594925efa11847a","before":"  protected override _onBeforeShow(): void {
    this._initSwipe()
  }","after":"  protected override _onBeforeShow(): void {
    this._initSwipe()
    const closeBtn = this._element.querySelector('[data-bs-dismiss="drawer"]')
    if (closeBtn) {
      closeBtn.focus({ preventScroll: true })
    }
  }"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"Upon opening any drawer, focus moves to the dismiss button, allowing keyboard users to immediately press Tab to navigate into the drawer's content and interact with form controls.","functional_risks":["If a drawer lacks a dismiss button with data-bs-dismiss="drawer", the focus attempt is safely skipped due to the null check.","The focus change occurs after swipe initialization, preserving existing touch/swipe behavior."],"verification_requirements":["After activating the filters button with Enter, the active element must be the drawer's close button (data-bs-dismiss="drawer").","Subsequent Tab presses must move focus to the first focusable element in the drawer (e.g., #in-stock checkbox), then through other controls.","Pressing Space on a checkbox must toggle its checked state.","Pressing Enter on the 'Show results' button must update the applied filter output and close the drawer.","Pressing Escape must close the drawer and return focus to the trigger button."]}
